WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.690
Speaker 1: Let's talk now about 2024 Republican
presidential candidate Chris Christie.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:09.120
The reason I talk about Chris Christie is
not because all of a sudden I'm a Republican.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.889
The reason I talk about Chris Christie is
not because I think he's going to win the

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:14.060
Republican nomination.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.129
I will get to that in a moment.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:22.651
The reason I talk about Chris Christie is
because the contrast between a Republican

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:29.369
who is connected to the real world, but whom
I disagree with on policy and the rest of

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:33.760
these clowns could not be a starker contrast
today.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.910
Chris Christie appeared on Fox News a couple
of days ago and it is remarkable.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.700
Yes, he's pounding Trump.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.750
He's going after Trump, he's ridiculing Trump.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.050
He's saying things about Trump that the rest
of them aren't willing to say.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:54.940
But it is remarkable how different his entire
demeanor and approach is to this Republican

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.260
primary.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.000
He's almost certainly not going to win.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.660
And we'll talk about that in a moment.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:05.320
But listen to Christie say things that are
not controversial and say them in a way that

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:10.000
they all should be saying them, but nobody's
willing to do it other than Chris Christie.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.490
Speaker 2: But my view is he's let us down,
Didn't build the wall.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.479
Mexico didn't pay for it.

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:16.560
Didn't repeal and replace Obamacare.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.979
He said he would say he's going to balance
the budget.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:19.979
He didn't.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:20.979
And you mentioned debates.

00:01:20.979 --> 00:01:24.480
Look, we should have debates and everyone
should be at the debates and folks should

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.460
go to Chris Christie dot com donate and make
sure I'm on the stage.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.710
But Donald Trump should be on that stage,
too.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.910
If you want the Republican nomination, the
Republican voters have the right to see us

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:38.750
right in those cameras and have us compare
and then let them choose.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.390
And American people are good at that.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.759
And we live, but they need all the information
and that's what we want to give them.

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:48.979
The fact is, if you put much stock into the
polling, what I put, that's what it is today.

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:50.590
You know, you're what they ask you, how they
ask those questions.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.299
You would call by pollster, they say, if the
election were held today.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:57.469
Well, if the election were held today, I'd
be shocked because the first election is not

00:01:57.469 --> 00:01:59.979
going to be in January in Iowa.

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:00.979
January of 2024.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:03.040
We're six, seven months away from that now.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.230
So let's run a campaign.

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:08.660
I don't think we crown kings in America.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.830
You got to work for it.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:13.849
And Donald Trump needs to work for this nominee,
become the nominee.

00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:15.160
Do you all become friends again?

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.520
Does he offer you a cabinet post again?

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.970
Do you all clean this up and he becomes the
nominee?

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.030
I don't think so.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:26.050
I think, you know, some of the some of the
stuff he's called me over the last few months,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:27.890
I don't think that's going to happen.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.840
And and that's sad.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.340
But it is the truth of the matter and it's
his doing.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.010
